speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, may I direct a question to the right hon. Prime Minister arising out of a speech made by the Minister of Industry, Trade and Commerce before the Mid-America World Trade Conference in Chicago. According to the release from the minister's office the minister is quoted as saying;
Canada will remain one of the most open and secure locations for investment by non-residents.
I want to ask the Prime Minister whether the statement that Canada will remain one of the most open locations for investment by non-residents is government policy, and whether this is the policy which has been adopted by the government with respect to foreign ownership?
